Interop harnesses: mimid against Haven's mimi-core and mimi-hubd
(github.com/havenmessenger/interop). Findings are tracked in beads under
mimid-1wgh.46.1 (protocol-06, Haven 2c14e62) and mimid-1wgh.46.6
(protocol-07, Haven 07ce96f), not here. None of this runs in CI: it builds third-party
code and, for the live run, starts servers.

To give a live mimid's local users KeyPackages for peers to fetch, see
../seed/README.

The opposite direction (Haven-encoded messages decoded by mimid) is an
ordinary offline test: crates/mimi-protocol/tests/haven_fixtures.rs.

Layout
  harness/      standalone crate (own [workspace]): Haven's mimi-core, pinned
                to a Haven commit in Cargo.toml, decodes mimid-encoded
                protocol-07 messages, compares fields, re-encodes, and checks
                byte identity. Extra modes: make-kp, make-kp-default (Haven
                mints KeyPackages), decode-commit (Haven's update-lane
                Commit decoders), decode-proposal (Haven's reader for a
                leaving member's proposal, with its ProposalRef).
  mimid-dump/   zz_dump_for_haven.rs, a mimi-protocol test that writes the
                mimid-encoded messages. It is a template: copy it into
                crates/mimi-protocol/tests/ to run it, then delete it.
  unicode/      standalone crate (own [workspace]): the Unicode stress tests
                (bead mimid-1wgh.54: Big List of Naughty Strings, hand-written
                cases, all four normalization forms) through Haven's
                mimi-core at the pinned commit, cross-checked byte for byte
                against mimid's mimi-content and mimi-room-policy. Run
                `cargo test -- --nocapture --test-threads=1` for the report.
                tests/joint.rs decodes the joint IETF 127 vector set
                (crates/mimid-server/tests/fixtures/joint-ietf127) with
                Haven's decoders and checks the file's claims about them.
  probe/        standalone crate: a short read-only check of Jason's public
                hub (mimi.havenmessenger.com) and its table seed, run from
                the mimid host (below)
  live/         the live run of mimid's PeerClient against mimi-hubd:
    run.sh        builds mimi-hubd from $HAVEN, makes a throwaway CA, and
                  enters an unprivileged user+network namespace (unshare)
    up.sh         (inside) starts mimi-hubd as haven.localhost on
                  127.0.0.1:8443 with mTLS, and socat on haven.localhost:443,
                  which presents a haven.localhost certificate and forwards
                  with the client certificate; sets SSL_CERT_FILE; runs the
                  given command
    selftest.sh   the proxy path works without a client certificate, and the
                  hub refuses direct access
    public.sh     runs b4.sh on the mimid host against a public hub (below)
    b4.sh         (inside) seeds Haven over its JSON lane (a Haven-minted
                  and a mimid-minted KeyPackage, consent, the room's first
                  participant) and its store (an enrolled handle: no route
                  does that), runs the driver, checks what the hub stored,
                  and copies mimid's Commits and leave proposal to out/
    certs.sh      throwaway CA and certificates; the client certificate
                  names b.example, the driver's provider domain, because
                  mimi-hubd checks the From header and the /notify source
                  against it (protocol-07 §4.1, §5.5)
    driver/       standalone crate: mimid crates by relative path, plus a copy
                  of the root Cargo.toml [patch] section (keep the two in step).
                  Mode make-kp <uri> <file> writes a mimid KeyPackage
                  Mode unicode: the hub half of the Unicode tests (bead
                  mimid-1wgh.54; src/unicode.rs): identifierQuery for
                  non-ASCII enrolled names and for every naughty string,
                  reportAbuse notes and consent keys read back from the
                  hub's store. Needs HUB_DB_CMD. Run it on the mimid host
                  as public.sh runs b4.sh, against our copy of the hub.

Why a namespace and port 443: mimi-hubd builds its directory URLs as
https://{provider_domain}, with no port (havenmessenger/interop#3). The
namespace lets socat own haven.localhost:443 without root.

Requirements: cargo, openssl, socat, unshare with unprivileged user
namespaces, curl.

Variables
  MIMID   this repository's root
  HAVEN   a checkout of github.com/havenmessenger/interop (live run only)
  HAVEN_TARGET  CARGO_TARGET_DIR for building mimi-hubd from $HAVEN (run.sh)
  CACHE   ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}; use private CARGO_TARGET_DIRs
          under it, not a shared target directory

Offline cross-check: mimid encodes, Haven decodes
  export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target
  export MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS=$CACHE/mimid-haven-vectors
  H=$MIMID/tools/interop/haven
  # 1. Haven mints a KeyPackage (diagnostic input)
  (cd $H/harness && cargo run -q -- make-kp $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS)
  # 2. mimid encodes the messages
  cp $H/mimid-dump/zz_dump_for_haven.rs $MIMID/crates/mimi-protocol/tests/
  (cd $MIMID && cargo test -p mimi-protocol --all-features --test zz_dump_for_haven)
  rm $MIMID/crates/mimi-protocol/tests/zz_dump_for_haven.rs
  # 3. Haven decodes them
  (cd $H/harness && cargo run -q -- $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS $MIMID/crates/mimi-mls/tests/fixtures/mlswg)

Live run
  export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-live-target
  (cd $H/live/driver && cargo build)
  # A Haven-minted KeyPackage with openmls's default lifetime and no GREASE
  # (see mimid-1wgh.46.1.13); the test helper's unbounded lifetime is refused
  # by mimid (RFC 9420 section 7.2).
  (cd $H/harness && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target \
     cargo run -q -- make-kp-default $MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS)
  cd $H/live
  HAVEN=... ./run.sh ./selftest.sh
  HAVEN=... DRIVER=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/debug/mimid-haven-live \
     KP=$MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS/haven_default_key_package.bin ./run.sh ./b4.sh
  # Haven's own decoders on mimid's Commits and leave proposal:
  (cd $H/harness && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target \
     cargo run -q -- decode-commit $H/live/out/update_commit.bin)
  (cd $H/harness && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-haven-xcheck-target \
     cargo run -q -- decode-proposal $H/live/out/leave_proposal.bin)

Live run against a public hub (bead mimid-1wgh.46.6)
  The driver and b4.sh take their names from the environment (defaults are
  the namespace run's): HAVEN_DOMAIN, OWN_DOMAIN, RUN_TAG (appended to every
  user and room name, so reruns against a hub that keeps state start fresh),
  HAVEN_BASE_URL (driver), HAVEN_LANE, CURL_OPTS, HUB_DB_CMD (b4.sh).
  public.sh runs B4 from this dev box on the mimid hackathon host, whose
  outbound proxy adds mimid's client certificate for haven.reviewcommit.com,
  and reaches the hub's store directly from the mimid host over SSH, with a
  key (/home/admin/interop/hubdb_ed25519) that the hub host's
  authorized_keys limits to the mimid host's address and one forced command,
  sqlite3 on the hub's database with the SQL on stdin, against a pinned host
  key (/home/admin/interop/known_hosts_hub). No SSH agent is forwarded. The
  hub host's security group allows port 22 from the mimid host only.
  public.sh changes no configuration on either host. Logs (b4 output, the
  hub's journal, the proxy's wire capture) go to live/out/public-<tag>/.
  (cd $H/live/driver && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/data/cargo/interop07-public-target cargo build --release)
  cd $H/live && DRIVER=/data/cargo/interop07-public-target/release/mimid-haven-live \
     KP=$MIMID_HAVEN_VECTORS/haven_default_key_package.bin ./public.sh

Probe of Haven's public hub (IETF 127 table)
  probe/ checks mimi.havenmessenger.com as seeded for the table
  (havenmessenger/interop#1): the directory; keyMaterial for erin as
  mimid's alice, which uses up one of erin's KeyPackages; keyMaterial for
  grace, who has none; identifierQuery for the handle erin and an unknown
  one. It writes nothing else. It runs on the mimid host, whose outbound
  proxy (mimi.havenmessenger.com is 127.0.0.2 in its /etc/hosts) adds
  mimid's client certificate. Expected on Haven's hub as of 2026-11-14:
  grace's answer is refused (mimid-1wgh.46.1.7), and identifierQuery
  answers a bare 200 or 404 (mimid-1wgh.46.6.3).
  (cd $H/probe && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/data/cargo/mimid-haven-live-target cargo build --release)
  scp -i ~/.ssh/mimid-hackathon.pem -o BatchMode=yes \
     /data/cargo/mimid-haven-live-target/release/haven-probe admin@172.31.40.235:/home/admin/interop/
  ssh -i ~/.ssh/mimid-hackathon.pem -o BatchMode=yes admin@172.31.40.235 \
     SSL_CERT_FILE=/home/admin/interop/trust.pem /home/admin/interop/haven-probe

The driver covers every PeerClient call Haven's directory offers: directory,
keyMaterial, submitMessage, update (one change; Add beside the change; two
changes; a member's leave as proposals, a Commit leaving them out, and the
Commit including them by reference), notify, requestConsent, updateConsent,
identifierQuery and reportAbuse. Haven offers no groupInfo (DIV-1).

Haven-encoded fixtures (the other direction) are regenerated with the
generator in crates/mimi-protocol/tests/fixtures/haven/gen; its PROVENANCE
has the command.

Generated files (vectors, out/, target/) are ignored by git.
